# Deployment and Docker

- Topology: Browser → Next.js standalone → Prisma → PostgreSQL 16. One-shot `migrations` runs the schema rollout approval gate, `db-push-safe`, and optional seed. App waits for that service, not merely `started`.
- One root `.env`. Helpers: `bash scripts/docker-dev.sh|docker-uat.sh|docker-prod.sh <command>`. No `.env.uat` / `.env.production`. Copy `.env.example` placeholders only.
- Set `TZ=Asia/Bangkok` for application containers and PostgreSQL session/database defaults in every environment. Persist dates and timestamps using Bangkok calendar/wall-clock semantics; do not convert stored values to UTC. Keep explicit application conversions so browser/device timezone cannot change persisted values.
- Compose: `docker-compose.yml` (dev), `docker-compose.uat.yml`, `docker-compose.prod.yml` + shared DB compose. Secrets files `postgres_user`, `postgres_password`, `postgres_db` — never commit values.
- Verify effective ports in Compose. DEPLOYMENT.md: dev host 3777→3000, UAT 3001, prod 3002, Postgres often 5437. `document/process/docker.md` may list 3000/5432 — do not assume; read the running mapping.
- Health: container `GET /api/health` every 30s after 40s start. Success 200 `database: connected`; failure 503.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ENV` is baked at build; rebuild to change. `RUN_SEED` / `SEED_PATH` control migration seed.
- Persist volume `pms-postgres-data-${APP_ENV}` via `POSTGRES_DATA_DIR` (default `./database/postgres/data`). Do not commit data files.
- Prod start/stop/restart/rebuild/init require confirmation. Optional profiles: `backup`, and prod-only `https` for nginx. `docker-prod.sh start` enables `https` when certificate files already exist. It does not issue a certificate. `docker-prod.sh stop` includes the profile so nginx is removed with the stack.
- Host budget on a shared 1 vCPU / 2 GB box: ~0.5 CPU and ~768 MB for this stack. The prod `https` profile adds nginx at 0.05 CPU and 64 MB and stays off until certificate files exist. Prisma `connection_limit=5`, Node heap 256 MB. Do not run two heavy `pnpm dev` stacks.
- After deploy: app + Postgres up, migrations exit 0, health 200, and a real Work Items / Daily Work record. Production HTTPS is nginx in the `https` profile: public 80/443, app and PostgreSQL stay on loopback. Issue and renew with `sudo bash infra/certbot/setup-https.sh`.
